ENGINE FACTS (src/PtolC_unicode, STATE_VERSION 6; monad.c, tokenizer.c, dprint.h):
- address (monad_word_coords): bijective Horner over the build's alphabet, wrap mod 2^64, `if (v>0) v--`; seed64 = v*0x9E3779B97F4A7C15; idx = (seed64*N)>>64 with N=25000; E = d* + (seed64>>11)/2^53*(Ω-d*). Slot and E come from ONE seed, so E is not independent. The bin stores NO per-word σ (zeros are generated by Newton; every seated word sits at zeros[slot]; σ=½ is only a printed constant).
- learn (monad_learn_ex): sentences end at . ! ? newline (+CJK ends), <2 bytes skipped; tokens <2 letters dropped (Han singles allowed); token_accept filter (hex, max length, vowel...); β accumulates in the slot: nb = β + E²·ALPHA_LEARN·|sin γ|·π/2, saturating; THE SLOT LABEL GOES TO THE WORD WITH THE HIGHER E (`if (!present || E > vocab[idx].E)`), not to the first word; A-edges inside a 12-token window within a sentence.
- builds: -DALPHABET_ASCII95 (English); -DALPHABET_TABLE -DALPHABET_HEADER=... (zh = 97,518 Han; un = ' a–z + Han = 97,545; fi); NEW -DHAN_RUN = a run of Han chars is one token, the filtered corpus is segmented by longest match over the list. Ground file must exist before -c/-l (else ingest saves to the protected default); run with HOME set to a throwaway dir.
